Author: CusDeb OS Team
Description: uxtheme: Keep the sign of negative theme integers.
 The scan for the first digit of an integer property skipped a leading
 minus sign, so negative values were read as positive. Mizu's Start button
 ContentMargins = -82, 95 thus put the button image inside the button,
 where it showed once the button got wider at a higher DPI.
 The fix applies at any DPI; at 96 DPI the affected Mizu parts (caption
 buttons, task band group menu) are not drawn in CDEX.
Last-Modified: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 14:50:00 +0300

--- a/src/dlls/uxtheme/msstyles.c
+++ b/src/dlls/uxtheme/msstyles.c
@@ -1361,7 +1361,7 @@
     LONG total = 0;
     BOOL gotNeg = FALSE;
 
-    while(cur < lpStringEnd && (*cur < '0' || *cur > '9' || *cur == '-')) cur++;
+    while(cur < lpStringEnd && *cur != '-' && (*cur < '0' || *cur > '9')) cur++;
     if(cur >= lpStringEnd) {
         return FALSE;
     }
